=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play ssh/ufw-session-out -------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: ssh/ufw-session-out$
# ufw allows 22 from 198.51.100.0/24 alone; the session is from$
# 192.0.2.10.$
$
# SSH ##########################################################$
$
  [ ] SSH                  Partial root key-only$
                             ~ Default port (22)$
$
  SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Key only sshd's default$
   -  Password Login       Off by sshd_config$
   -  SSH Port             22$
   -  Allowed Users        Anyone$
   -  Brute-Force Limit    On sshd's default$
   -  Logged in as         george, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disallow root login  Root can't log in over SSH$
   2) Password login on    Let passwords log in again$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22$
   6) SSH keys             3 keys, 2 to review$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3, 6 or q]: 3$
$
# Warning$
# No ufw rule for port 22 covers 192.0.2.10, where you're logged$
# in from. You couldn't reach the new port. Add a rule for it$
# first.$
$
# SSH ##########################################################$
$
  [ ] SSH                  Partial root key-only$
                             ~ Default port (22)$
$
  SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Key only sshd's default$
   -  Password Login       Off by sshd_config$
   -  SSH Port             22$
   -  Allowed Users        Anyone$
   -  Brute-Force Limit    On sshd's default$
   -  Logged in as         george, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disallow root login  Root can't log in over SSH$
   2) Password login on    Let passwords log in again$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22$
   6) SSH keys             3 keys, 2 to review$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3, 6 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

